{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969949-abyssal-claimed","id":969949,"title":"Abyssal-Claimed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-15T08:51:42-07:00","id":969949,"title":"Abyssal-Claimed","content":"So, how would you model people and objects Claimed (as per the Claim Manifestation) by Abyssals (Gulmoth, mostly, but potentially Acamoth too)?<br /> <br /> Any special rulings used? Examples anyone wants to post? Cults/Organizations that do this deliberately?<br /> <br /> Example Ruling:<br /> Abyss-Claimed beings register as a Sleeper with the Liar merit, even when it would otherwise not make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T13:07:38-07:00","id":970138,"title":"","content":"I love this idea and may just toy with it in future.<br /> <br /> The closest example I have is when a group of players of mine fought the leader of a Gate cult and disrupted a ritual that ended up turning the leader into a horrible, cancerous flesh flower. Not sure that quite counts.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Claimed would be horrifying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:28:40-07:00","id":970228,"title":"","content":"AFAIK, both of those entities are generally way too big (rank-wise) to neatly fit into a single fleshy vessel. You could try it with abyssal incursions, mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:36:31-07:00","id":970238,"title":"","content":"Gulmoth are just abyssals living in the abyss, summoned here. Acamoth are stuck here for one reason or another. Either can be Rank 1.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see some Abyssal-Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T14:42:52-07:00","id":970242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969949-abyssal-claimed?p=970238#post970238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gulmoth are just abyssals living in the abyss, summoned here. Acamoth are stuck here for one reason or another. Either can be Rank 1.<br /> <br /> It would be interesting to see some Abyssal-Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div> That changed in 2e, now Acamoths are Abyssal creatures in Goetic Form and Gulmoths are Abyssal Creatures in Spirit or Ghost Form. Or the other way around, I'll check later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T15:44:08-07:00","id":970280,"title":"","content":"It didn't change, it just made it clear that they use the Ephemeral Creature rules, Acamoth use the goetic variant specifically.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12191_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12191\" data-vbnamecard=\"12191\">Malus</a> That isn't an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:42:24-07:00","id":970342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Axelgear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969949-abyssal-claimed?p=970138#post970138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I love this idea and may just toy with it in future.<br /> <br /> The closest example I have is when a group of players of mine fought the leader of a Gate cult and disrupted a ritual that ended up turning the leader into a horrible, cancerous flesh flower. Not sure that quite counts.<br /> <br /> Abyssal Claimed would be horrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/236x/2b/7f/1c/2b7f1c12effc53fa11c5f9ded2654d52.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> Just replace Cthulhu with the Prince of 10,000 Leaves.<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T18:58:43-07:00","id":970387,"title":"","content":"Funnily enough, I'm planning on using something like Abyssal Claimed in a game I'm running tonight. Inspired by various media, I'm doing a &quot;cut off island&quot; that the players group can explore thanks to a friendly Walker in the Mists (the island is enshrouded in a fog which people become lost in and can't penetrate but the walker in mists can pass through). Inside a Scelestus, attempting to become an archmage, has performed a ritual that has killed everyone with willpower four or less to empower himself. Those that died are then claimed by minor abyssal spirits that then rise and continue slaughtering the islands inhabitants. The reason I'm using Abyssal Claimed is so that, as the game goes on, the enemies the players encounter will become increasingly stranger and dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:00:32-07:00","id":974250,"title":"","content":"Abyssal creatures are supposed to invert rules systems and have contradictions in them. Someone had a good example of an Abyssal spirit of betrayal whose ban was to never betray anyone. So I would argue for something radically different than a normal claimed. There are a lot of ephemeral entities in the Chronicles of Darkness. Sadly too many of them are described as having &quot;Alien intelligences&quot; which &quot;aren't comprehensible to humans&quot;, they are often &quot;Single Minded&quot; etc. It kind of just seems like the same thing after awhile.<br /> <br /> For any abyssal claiming, it would have to be compared as somehow worse than the many many terrible claimings (and similar things) that could happen in the Chronicles of Darkness. Just spirits alone have huge potential to be horrifying. Beasts, Geists, Demons, Angels, Inferno Demons, Strix, Exiles, Ghosts etc. all have these creepy aspects of body stealing, possession, and being consumed by a supernatural force. I think the abyss, due to its &quot;anti-reality&quot; nature, should have something different than this very large set of phenomena.<br /> <br /> My idea:<br /> <br /> When an Abyssal spirit claims a human, the abyssal spirit loses its identity and empowers the possessed to become a Proximus-type lesser template capable of various Abyssal talents. The personality of the human will change radically, but it is ultimately them in control.<br /> <br /> The idea is that unlike normal spirits, which are beyond selfish, an abyssal spirit is altruistically giving up its identity and will to help spread the abyss through its version of the claiming manifestation. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8619-aforgeforthoughts","name":"AForgeForThoughts","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T06:55:55-07:00","id":974383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AForgeForThoughts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969949-abyssal-claimed?p=974250#post974250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Abyssal creatures are supposed to invert rules systems and have contradictions in them. Someone had a good example of an Abyssal spirit of betrayal whose ban was to never betray anyone. So I would argue for something radically different than a normal claimed. There are a lot of ephemeral entities in the Chronicles of Darkness. Sadly too many of them are described as having &quot;Alien intelligences&quot; which &quot;aren't comprehensible to humans&quot;, they are often &quot;Single Minded&quot; etc. It kind of just seems like the same thing after awhile.<br /> <br /> For any abyssal claiming, it would have to be compared as somehow worse than the many many terrible claimings (and similar things) that could happen in the Chronicles of Darkness. Just spirits alone have huge potential to be horrifying. Beasts, Geists, Demons, Angels, Inferno Demons, Strix, Exiles, Ghosts etc. all have these creepy aspects of body stealing, possession, and being consumed by a supernatural force. I think the abyss, due to its &quot;anti-reality&quot; nature, should have something different than this very large set of phenomena.<br /> <br /> My idea:<br /> <br /> When an Abyssal spirit claims a human, the abyssal spirit loses its identity and empowers the possessed to become a Proximus-type lesser template capable of various Abyssal talents. The personality of the human will change radically, but it is ultimately them in control.<br /> <br /> The idea is that unlike normal spirits, which are beyond selfish, an abyssal spirit is altruistically giving up its identity and will to help spread the abyss through its version of the claiming manifestation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, I'm working on a group that lets/forces themselves to be Claimed by Abyssal entities (part &quot;keeping the demon caged&quot; and part &quot;fight fire with fire&quot;). They use a ritual to keep their human identity intact, and keep the Abyssal inert... most of the time. But they can leverage its power as long as they are willing to make it stronger and risk &quot;waking it up&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm still working on them, but I'll post it here once I've got more written down.<br /> <br /> But on your idea, that sounds like it could definitely serve as a weird one-off situation. Though I think most Abyssals are more consumed by <b><u><i>hate</i></u></b> for all that exists to be anywhere close to altruistic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T07:25:20-07:00","id":974400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969949-abyssal-claimed?p=974383#post974383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though I think most Abyssals are more consumed by <b><u><i>hate</i></u></b> for all that exists to be anywhere close to altruistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even so, Intruders may have very strange ideas on what constitutes harmful. More than that, one might even fall back on their &quot;higher nature&quot; and help its host to become something that doesn't need to be hated. Hatred and harm are connected in the Fallen, but in the Abyss it's unlikely to be that simple. An Intruder that loves you can be even more horrifying.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T17:37:19-07:00","id":974775,"title":"","content":"I think an even freaker question is can an Abyssal Giest make deal with a dead mortal to create an Abyssal Sin Eater?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T18:26:31-07:00","id":974797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969949-abyssal-claimed?p=974775#post974775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think an even freaker question is can an Abyssal Giest make deal with a dead mortal to create an Abyssal Sin Eater?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think there is an Abyssal-Ghost template. Possibly because Ghosts have Integrity and Virtues and Vices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}